      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Managed conservation is a fundamentally flawed, anthropocentric approach that treats nature as a resource to be curated for human benefit. This outdated model imposes human will onto complex ecological systems, often prioritizing aesthetic or utilitarian values over genuine ecological integrity. True rewilding recognizes that nature possesses its own inherent right to self-determination, requiring us to step back and allow natural processes to drive recovery. We must abandon the illusion of control and embrace the wildness that defines a healthy planet.",
      "source": "target",
